    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-u/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The test marks, x , of 20 students were coded and their results were summarized as   2 ( x − 10 ) = 220 and ( x − 10 ) = 2720 . a) Use a detailed method to show that  2 ( ) 9 x = 9120 . b) Calculate the mean and standard deviation of the test marks of these students. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:586.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) From P(x −10) = 220 [B1] [M1] [A1] we get X x = 220 + 20(10) . [M1] [A1] = 420 Expanding the second given sum gives 2720 = P x2 −20(420) + 100(20), [M1] [A1] so x2 = 9120 . X [M1] [A1] (b) Alternatively use y = x −10: √ q 2720/20 −112 = ¯y = 220/20 = 11, σy = 15. Decoding adds ten to the mean and leaves the standard deviation unchanged: The mean is 420/20 = 21 [M1] [A1] and the standard deviation is √ q 9120/20 −212 = 15 ≈3.873 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 13 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The test marks, x , of 20 students were coded and their results were summarized as   2 ( x − 10 ) = 220 and ( x − 10 ) = 2720 . a) Use a detailed method to show that  2 ( ) 9 x = 9120 . b) Calculate the mean and standard deviation of the test marks of these students. ( ) 4"
  },
