    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-u/q5",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A , B and C are defined in the same probability space so that P ( ) A = P ( ) C = P ( B ′ ∩ C ′ ) = 0.4 and       ( P A ∪ B ) = 0.58 . It is further given that A and B are independent, and A and C are mutually exclusive.  ′ ′ ′ ′  ( ) 9 Find the value of P  ( B ∩ C ) ∪ ( B ∩ C ∩ A ) .\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Independence gives P(A ∪B) = 0.4 + 0.6 P(B) , [B1] [A1] = 0.58 so P(B) = 0.3 [A1] and P(A ∩B) = 0.12. [A1] The partition of C′ gives P(B ∩C′) = 0.6 −0.4 . [A1] = 0.2\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Because A ⊆C′ up to a null event, P(A ∩B′ ∩C′) = 0.4 −0.12 . [A1] = 0.28 Hence P(B′ ∩C′ ∩A′) = 0.4 −0.28 . [A1] = 0.12 The remaining Venn regions can also be found explicitly: B ∩C has probability 0.30 −0.20 = 0.10; C only has 0.40 −0.10 = 0.30. Within C′ the B-only region outside A is 0.20 −0.12 = 0.08. The two requested sets are disjoint, giving 0.32 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 9 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The events A , B and C are defined in the same probability space so that P ( ) A = P ( ) C = P ( B ′ ∩ C ′ ) = 0.4 and       ( P A ∪ B ) = 0.58 . It is further given that A and B are independent, and A and C are mutually exclusive.  ′ ′ ′ ′  ( ) 9 Find the value of P  ( B ∩ C ) ∪ ( B ∩ C ∩ A ) ."
  },
