    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-u/q6",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q6-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The sale records in &quot;Laptop World&quot;, show that 35% of its customers buy insurance when they purchase a laptop. A sample of 160 customers is considered. The probability that less than x customers will buy insurance with their laptop purchase is 4.09% . Determine the value of x . ( 10 )\" style=\"--madas-width:586.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q6-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Under the binomial model, X ∼B(160, 0.35) [B1] [A1] with mean 56 and variance 36.4. [M1] [A1] Approximate by Y ∼N(56, 36.4). [M1] [A1] Since X &lt; x means X ≤x −1, [A1] the corrected boundary is x −0.5. [A1] The parameters are np = 160(0.35) = 56 and np(1 −p) = 56(0.65) . = 36.4\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Invert the normal CDF to get x −0.5 = 56 −1.74 36.4, approximately 45.5. Thus x −0.5 −56 √ = Φ−1(0.0409) ≈−1.74, x = 46 . [M1] [A1] 36.4 Source clarification. The given percentage comes from the continuity-corrected normal approximation: The exact binomial probability P(X &lt; 46) is about 3.92%.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The sale records in \"Laptop World\", show that 35% of its customers buy insurance when they purchase a laptop. A sample of 160 customers is considered. The probability that less than x customers will buy insurance with their laptop purchase is 4.09% . Determine the value of x . ( 10 )"
