    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-u/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A box contains 3 black balls and 7 white balls, all identical in size. An experiment consists of drawing a ball out of the box and recording its colour. • If the ball drawn is black, after its colour is recorded, the ball is replaced back into the box and an extra black ball is also placed in the box. • If the ball drawn is white, after its colour is recorded, the ball is not replaced back into the box. The experiment is attempted 3 consecutive times. Given that in these 3 attempts both colours were recorded, determine the probability that a black colour was recorded twice. ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:449.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Write B, W for a black or white draw: [B1] [A1] Updating the counts after each draw gives the mixed-colour probabilities Sequence BBW BWB WBB BWW WBW WWB [B1] [A1] Probability 7/110 21/275 7/75 63/550 7/50 7/40 For example P(BBW) = (3/10)(4/11)(7/12). [A1] The other path products, in table order after BBW, are (3/10)(7/11)(4/10), (7/10)(3/9)(4/10), (3/10)(7/11)(6/10), (7/10)(3/9)(6/10), and (7/10)(6/9)(3/8). The first three entries total 7/30, and all six total 175/264. [A1] The conditional probability is (7/30)/(175/264) = 44/125 = 0.352 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A box contains 3 black balls and 7 white balls, all identical in size. An experiment consists of drawing a ball out of the box and recording its colour. • If the ball drawn is black, after its colour is recorded, the ball is replaced back into the box and an extra black ball is also placed in the box. • If the ball drawn is white, after its colour is recorded, the ball is not replaced back into the box. The experiment is attempted 3 consecutive times. Given that in these 3 attempts both colours were recorded, determine the probability that a black colour was recorded twice. ( ) 8 "
