    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Drawing a diagram: Integrate a = 4t −9 to get v = 2t2 −9t + C. From v(1) = −3, C = 4.\" style=\"--madas-width:441.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The minimum occurs at t = 9/4, where v = −49/8 m s−1 . [M1] Integrate acceleration [M1] apply the initial condition [M1] set acceleration to zero [B1] identify the minimum time [M1] substitute into the velocity (b) v = (2t −1)(t −4) [B1] = 0 at t = 0.5 and t = 4 . [M1] [A1] (c) An antiderivative is F(t) = 2t3/3 −9t2/2 + 4t. [B1] [A1] The source also uses direct integration over three intervals: R 1/2 R 4 R 9/2 Distance is v dt − 1/2 v dt + v dt, since only the middle integral has negative velocity. 0 4\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q9-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The velocity signs are +, −, +. [M1] [A1] Summing absolute displacements gives 2F(0.5) −2F(4) + F(4.5) = 389/24 m ≈16.21 m . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 15 marks.</p>"
