  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-u/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"B T a A θ O A uniform rod AB , of length 2a , is resting with its end A on rough horizontal ground and a point T on the rod in contact with a rough fixed prism of semicircular cross-section, of radius a . The rod lies in a vertical plane which is perpendicular to the axis of the prism, as shown in the figure above.\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The coefficient of friction between the rod and the ground at A and between the rod and the prism at T , is µ , 0 &lt; µ &lt; . 1 3 When the rod is inclined at an angle θ to the horizontal, where tan θ = , the rod is at 4 the point of slipping. Determine the value of µ . ( 12 )\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a good diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:564.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let the rod have weight W, and denote the ground and prism normal forces by R, N. [M1] The prism reaction is perpendicular to the rod since OT is a radius to the tangent point. [A1] In right triangle ATO, AT = a cot θ = 4a/3 . [A1] Taking moments about A gives N(4a/3) = Wa cos θ, [M1] so N = 3W/5. [A1] At impending slip, friction at A acts towards O and friction at T acts up the rod: [A1] With cos θ = 4/5 and sin θ = 3/5, [A1] the balances are R + N(4/5) + µN(3/5) = W, µR + µN(4/5) = N(3/5). [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q11-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Substitute N = 3W/5 in the vertical balance to obtain R/W = (13 −9µ)/25. Horizontal balance becomes µ(13 −9µ)/25 + 12µ/25 = 9/25. Multiply by 25 and collect powers of µ. Eliminating R, N gives 9µ2 −25µ + 9 = 0. [A1] Only the smaller root satisfies 0 &lt; µ &lt; 1, [A1] so √ µ = (25 − 301)/18 ≈0.425 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
