      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-u/q13-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Take downwards as positive: The load inside the lift satisfies 80g −768 = 80a. [B1] [A1] Thus 784 −768 = 80a, which gives a = 0.2 m s−2 downwards: [A1] The support on the load is 768 N upwards; its equal and opposite reaction on the lift is internal to the combined system: Hence this pair disappears in the second force balance: For the whole lift and load, the weights act downwards and the two external forces F and 4500 act upwards: [A1] Newton’s second law gives 400g + 80g −F −4500 = (80 + 400)a. [A1] Substituting gives 480g −F −4500 = 480(0.2), or 204 −F = 96. [M1] Hence F = 108 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
